╭──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
│  monochange init                                         │
│  Generate monochange.toml with detected packages         │
╰──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯

▸ Description

  Scans the workspace for supported package manifests (Cargo.toml, package.json, deno.json, pubspec.yaml) and generates a monochange.toml configuration file with discovered packages, version groups, and default CLI commands.

  Use --provider to scaffold source-control integration (GitHub, GitLab, Gitea, Forgejo) with release automation CLI commands.

▸ Usage

  monochange init [OPTIONS]

▸ Options

  --force               Overwrite an existing monochange.toml file
  --provider <PROVIDER>  Source-control provider (github, gitlab, gitea)

▸ Examples

  Initialize a fresh workspace:
    monochange init

  Overwrite existing config:
    monochange init --force

  Initialize with GitHub integration:
    monochange init --provider github

  Initialize with GitLab integration:
    monochange init --provider gitlab

  Initialize with Gitea integration:
    monochange init --provider gitea

▸ Tips

  • Run monochange init at the root of your monorepo.
  • The generated config is a starting point — customize packages, groups, and CLI commands in monochange.toml.
  • Use --provider=github to get GitHub Actions workflow templates included.

▸ See Also

  monochange help populate  monochange help step validate  monochange help discover


